{
  "dom_id": "step-q110213",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The fee a plumber charges for a callout is given by the expression $45h+50,$ where $h$ is the time, in hours, it takes him to complete the job. \n\nWhat does the constant term of the expression represent in this context?",
  "worked_solution": "The expression tells us that the plumber charges $$45$ every hour, plus a 'base fee' of $$50.$ \n\nThe constant term is $50.$ This represents the fee (in dollars) the plumber charges for working zero hours.",
